  ],
  "spec": {
    "ratio": "16:9",
    "duration": 15,
    "resolution": "1080p",
    "audio": "on"
  },
  "style_lock": "Lock the painterly anime illustrated style of all reference images across every frame — hand-drawn line work, painterly cel-shading, deep violet and warm orange palette. Every single frame must look like an illustrated animation. The video must never resemble live-action footage."
}

What this does differently from the timestamp version

Reference Mode role declarations upfront — references block tells the engine what each image is for

One primary action + one camera move per shot — every shot block has exactly one action string and one camera movement

Spatial re-anchoring — every shot has a subject_position field that re-states where characters are in frame after each cut

Nested camera/scene/action/audio — the skill's JSON Structured format

Global block — environment and lighting stated once, applies across all shots, prevents drift

Style lock — pulled out as its own field at the end

This is the skill-compliant version. It's still attempting something past the engine's reliable range (15s, 9 beats), but the format is now correct for the complexity. Run it and see what comes back.

{
  "references": {
    "image_1": "first_frame — bright purple hallway, character on right side of frame, breathing hard, baseline state",
    "image_2": "last_frame — same hallway in dark blue-black tone, character on right in powered-up state, rim-lit by cyan vine glow",
    "image_3": "character identity reference — preserve face, beard, glasses, black Nike cap, and orange Nike sweatshirt across the entire shot"
  },
  "style": "Painted illustration style. Preserve the visual style of image 1 and image 2 across every frame.",
  "global": {
    "environment": "Magical castle hallway with stone walls, glowing vines on the ceiling, magenta orbs on the walls, cyan-pink ambient light shifting to deep blue-black across the shot.",
    "lighting": "Opens bright purple, transitions through violent flicker, settles into deep blue-black with only cyan vine glow and dim magenta orbs surviving.",
    "subject_anchor": "Character stays locked on the right side of frame throughout, body angled toward camera, holding position."
  },
  "shots": [
    {
      "shot": 1,
      "duration": "0:00–0:01",
      "anchor_image": "image_1",
      "camera": {
        "type": "tripod",
        "movement": "locked-off static",
        "framing": "medium shot, character right of frame"
      },
      "scene": {
        "subject_position": "character standing right of frame, body angled toward camera, breathing hard"
      },
      "action": "Character holds position, chest rising and falling from heavy breathing",
      "audio": "low ambient magical hum, heavy breath"
    },
    {
      "shot": 2,
      "duration": "0:01–0:02",
      "anchor_image": "image_3",
      "camera": {
        "type": "tripod",
        "movement": "locked-off static",
        "framing": "medium shot, character right of frame"
      },
      "scene": {
        "subject_position": "character right of frame, energy beginning to radiate from skin"
      },
      "action": "Shoulders broaden, chest expands, arms swell with muscle, orange Nike sweatshirt stretches and tears along shoulder seams. Cyan and magenta energy rim-lights his silhouette. Jaw clenches, breath turns to a low growl",
      "audio": "deep low-frequency rumble building, fabric ripping, sharp breath, energy crackle"
    },
    {
      "shot": 3,
      "duration": "0:02–0:04",
      "anchor_image": "image_3",
      "camera": {
        "type": "tripod",
        "movement": "locked-off static",
        "framing": "medium shot, character right of frame"
      },
      "scene": {
        "subject_position": "character holds powered-up stance right of frame, hallway lights flickering around him"
      },
      "action": "Hallway lights flicker violently, magenta orbs pulse and stutter, vine glow surges and dims. Each flicker holds dimmer than the last",
      "audio": "electrical buzz-out, glass hum, pulses of low bass with each flicker, silence between"
    },
    {
      "shot": 4,
      "duration": "0:04–0:05",
      "anchor_image": "image_2",
      "camera": {
        "type": "tripod",
        "movement": "locked-off static",
        "framing": "medium shot, character right of frame"
      },
      "scene": {
        "subject_position": "character holds pumped stance right of frame, rim-lit by surviving cyan vine glow"
      },
      "action": "Lights stabilize at their darkest setting. Character holds his powered-up pose, chest rising and falling. Final frame matches image 2 exactly",
      "audio": "low magical hum, slow heavy breathing, stillness"
    }
  ],
  "spec": {
    "ratio": "16:9",
    "duration": 5,
    "resolution": "1080p",
    "audio": "on"
  },
  "style_lock": "Locked-off static medium shot throughout — no pan, no zoom, no push. The transition is in lighting and character state, not camera. Preserve the painted illustration style of image 1 and image 2 across every frame. Character must remain on the right side of frame throughout."
}

Note on the compression: the original was 12s with 4 distinct beats. Cutting to 5s means each beat now gets ~1.25s. The transformation (shoulders broadening, fabric tearing) and the flicker sequence both happen faster — Seedance will handle this but the body change may feel rushed. If the result looks too jumpy, the cleanest fix is dropping the flicker beat entirely (Shot 3) and giving more time to the transformation itself.
